ef 17592186526057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166771 #edb/ref 1039 "Integrating Using Arcoth" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166771 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166771 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1c7d3082-d63a-5eac-9a9b-47681f8d4694" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1045 "Integration Using Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186167704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167022 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9f886d85-2df1-5f0a-8d7d-9ac4d46bc4e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186165321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167352 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95358" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167352 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167352 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int \\frac{e}{\\sqrt{3}(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|>1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b469e6a2-d596-5cc6-8ef7-9f2fb38722c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167352 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{e}{\\sqrt{3}(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{e}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{e}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167406 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186165644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167406 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95819" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167406 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167406 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2(1-{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167406 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fef2d4a0-63bd-50d5-be34-68f559ae65d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167406 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2(1-{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int -\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167601 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167601 #edb/ref 1061 31215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167601 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "39ddcb2e-7a38-5abc-b491-af74837bc920" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167601 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167602 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167602 #edb/ref 1061 31216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167602 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "acbc6382-12bf-5cfc-ad37-6f0b89b9fa84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167602 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167603 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167603 #edb/ref 1061 31217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167603 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b08bfe8b-9e44-5137-a3d9-56d3138b6315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167603 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167704 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167704 #edb/ref 1061 32698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167704 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "36d709c0-168f-57e9-9ba0-9651411edeb8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167704 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167712 #edb/ref 1061 32720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167712 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6157bd21-aca9-574c-a8ba-03e7aad7c93f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167712 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168094 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall the following derivatives of the inverse reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}, &  & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}, &  & \\,x\\in (0,1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}, &  & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince integration is the reverse of differentiation, we arrive at the following basic integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C, &  & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ) \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C, &  & \\,x\\in (0,1) \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C, &  & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now use these formulas for finding integrals. For example, let's find the integral\n\n$$\n\\int \\left(\\dfrac{2}{3x\\sqrt{1-x^2}} + \\cos x \\right) \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of integration and the formulas above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{2}{3x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168094 #edb/ref 1065 5213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168094 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "77d4740c-3cac-5695-aa67-597e3c0ce164" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168094 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168102 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that \n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2} \\,\\textrm{d}x = {\\color{blue}\\artanh{x}} + C, \\qquad {\\color{blue}x\\in(-1,1)}.\n$$\n\nBut we have just seen that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2} \\,\\textrm{d}x = {\\color{red}\\arcoth{x}} + C, \\qquad {\\color{red}x\\in(-\\infty,-1) \\cup (1,\\infty)}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the integral on the left-hand side is the same but we used different functions on the right. What is the difference, and how do we know which hyperbolic function to use?\n\nThe difference is the domain of the variable $x.$ When the $|x| < 1,$ we use the antiderivative $\\artanh{x},$ otherwise we use the antiderivative $\\arcoth{x}.$\n\nFor instance, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since the limits of integration lie in the interval $(-1,1),$ we used the antiderivative $\\artanh{x}.$\n\nWhile, on the other hand, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\,{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(3)-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since the limits of integration lie in the interval $(1,\\infty),$ we used the antiderivative $\\arcoth{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168102 #edb/ref 1065 5227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168102 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "169c2d19-f0a1-557e-88ed-519503440186" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168102 #edb/ref 1067 "The Importance of the Domain When Integrating Using Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525229 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{e}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525229 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525229 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a6390a2-c411-56f8-afd4-331308789c1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525240 #edb/ref 1080 "-2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525240 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525240 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0f47a5c2-0604-57c0-a510-d655fb160fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525248 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{8}+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525248 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525248 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "